{
 "encounter_id": "01005",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "FAMILY_MEMBER"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good morning. Before we start, Mr Mehta, or Arjun, or what would you like me to call you? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Arjun is fine, sir. Doctor. And this is my mother, she insisted, because the academy sent a letter. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "The ECG at the football academy was abnormal, doctor, they said I must see a heart doctor before he trains again, I haven't slept."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I understand, that letter would worry any parent. Arjun, tell me what you've noticed. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A bit dizzy, sometimes, after training. I have to sit down for a minute."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "When did that start?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "About a month ago."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Since March, doctor. That's three months. He didn't tell me."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Between one and three months, then. Anything else after training?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My heart races. Like it's beating in my throat."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Does it settle quickly? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A few minutes. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And breath?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "At the end of sprints I'm sort of gasping more than the others."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "And he's tired all the time, doctor, he sleeps on the bus."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Has he had chest pain?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No chest pain."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you ever fainted or nearly fainted?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, never fainted."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any blackouts at all, loss of memory?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No blackouts."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any breathlessness at rest?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, only when I'm pushing hard."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any swelling in your legs?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No swelling."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What do you take, Arjun?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ibuprofen, 400 mg, after matches, if my knee aches. And a protein powder, I buy it online, I can't remember the brand, it's the green tub."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "We'll look at the tub next time. Any allergies?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Wasp stings. I'm meant to be allergic. But I don't know what actually happened, I was a baby."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Nobody told us the details either. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll note wasp stings, reaction unknown. Medical history?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Asthma as a child. Hay fever. And low iron once."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A knee scope on the left, when I was seventeen."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any heart problems or sudden deaths in the family?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "My father's father had a heart attack at fifty. That's all we know."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check you. Pulse 48, blood pressure 118 over 70, temperature 36.5, oxygen 99 percent, breathing 12, weight 74 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Forty-eight? Is that dangerous? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "In a trained athlete it can be normal. Let me listen to his heart.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Do I take my shirt off? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Please. Heart sounds are normal, and the rhythm is regular, though slow."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Slow? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And I can hear a soft murmur, the sort that is often harmless in people who are fit."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A murmur? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any wheeze at the moment, Arjun?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any weakness or numbness in your arms or legs?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing like that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Here is my thinking. The slow pulse and the ECG pattern are very often athlete's heart, a normal adaptation to training. I think that is the most likely explanation."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Most likely? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes, but some conditions can look the same on an ECG, and with the dizziness, I won't take chances. For now, no hard training until a sports cardiologist has seen him."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "How long? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll write to the cardiologist today and ask for the earliest appointment. They'll decide what's needed. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Thank God. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Walking and gentle jogging are fine. If he faints or has chest pain, go to the emergency department at once."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "We will. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in two weeks, whatever the cardiologist says."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Two weeks. Thanks, doctor. ~"
  }
 ],
